  "about": "Places a remembered folder (folder for next time) or permission 3 (allow future sends into this folder) may never be: places that run things at sign-in or when a shell starts, places that hold keys, and the system's own folders (Security Design Part T). A folder is refused when it is one of these, inside one, or holds one (a sent folder path could reach it: a folder WindowsPowerShell saved into Documents becomes the PowerShell profile). Bases are found through the system's own known-folder lookup, never environment variables; when a base one of this system's places needs cannot be resolved, every folder is refused (what is there cannot be told). Bases: home, documents, appdata, localappdata, programdata, windir, programfiles, programfilesx86, root.",
